  "body": "Continuous C-axis live tooling, first shippable slice: the rotary kinds (Rotary Contour / Parallel / Offset) on a mill-turn whose spindle is C now generate, verify and post through the Fanuc lathe post, instead of refusing \"pinned (M13.5 B)\".\n\n## What changed\n\n- **cl**: `Move::rotary: Option<f64>`, the spindle's stated C in unwrapped degrees, beside the part-frame `to`/`axis`. `cl::stamp_c` (new `cl/rotary.rs`) stamps a radially posed part-frame path: C = minus the tip's azimuth (Rz(C) turns the tip onto the +X live-tool station), unwrapped move to move. Every move is split collinearly until the machine's X/Z/C-linear motion follows the verified chord within the op's tolerance. Refused by name: arcs, moves with no pose or a pose off the radial station, moves it cannot split near the spindle line, and paths carrying cycle/comp/thread/probe records. When the field is absent nothing changes: goldens, streams and project files stay byte-identical (the project field skips serialization).\n- **app**: the rotary letter gate now returns 'C' for the spindle line, and the three rotary arms stamp their path (`rotary_gate::stamp_spindle_c`, the line must be world Z). `machine::check_document` checks a C move for a rotary named C and its stated travel, and no longer reads the part-frame axis as A/B for it. `MoveDto.rotary` persists the angle.\n- **post stream/engine**: a C path writes `PARAM LiveTool radial` and `A 0 B 0 C <c>` on every move. The engine refuses that section by name for any script that does not declare `liveTooling = true` (same pattern as `coolantModes`), so every mill post refuses it.\n- **.mch grammar**: `tool_station.live_tool { c_axis_on, c_axis_off, spindle_on, spindle_off }`, the builder-specific engage and live-spindle words (all four or none), mirrored to `machine.liveTool`.\n- **fanuc-lathe.cps**: the C section. G98, the machine's C-on word, `<spindle_on> S<rpm>`. Every move is turned by C and must land on the station (5 um), otherwise it is refused and never projected. Output is `G01 X<2r> Z C F`, with F scaled for the control's composite rotary feed law (C degrees counted as mm). Rapids are G01 at the machine's stated max feed, never G00. The first move positions with `G00 C` and then `G00 X Z`. Arcs and cycles in the section are refused. Afterwards: spindle off, C off, G99. With no `live_tool` words stated, the section is refused by name.\n\n## Readings\n\n- The wrapped helix golden at r10, 30 deg chords, tol 0.01: each chord splits into 8 pieces. X dips to 19.318 at the chord midpoints, so the tool follows the planned chord, not an arc. F is about 2250-2370 for a 400 mm/min tip feed (composite degree-as-mm scaling).\n- The Rotary Contour on the standing r6/r5 bar (mill-turn C) generates with every move on the station, posts with zero warnings, and contains no M03.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `cl::rotary::tests::*` (3): unwrap, winding, refusals.\n- `c_axis_live.rs` (new, 4):\n  - `a_rotary_contour_on_the_spindle_states_c_on_every_move_and_posts`: generate + post.\n  - `the_wrapped_helix_posts_to_its_golden`: `golden/nc/fanuc-lathe/c_axis_helix.nc`.\n  - `every_post_without_c_or_without_the_machines_words_refuses_by_name`: mill post / no live_tool words / C disagreeing with XY.\n  - `the_c_word_rides_the_stream_and_parses_back`: also proves a path without C stays byte-shape identical.\n- `rotary_letter.rs`: the pinned test is replaced by `the_mill_turn_spindle_as_c_axis_answers_c_and_stamps_it`. `operation::rotary_gate` unit test updated the same way.\n- Touched suites run: see the PR comment for the gate readings.\n\n## Limits (owed on #33, see docs/decisions/33-continuous-c.md)\n\n- The machine C-sense word.\n- Unwinding C on links against a stated travel. The shipped millturn.mch states -360..360, so a multi-ring path is refused by the letter gate.\n- Axial/face live-tool stations and G12.1 polar interpolation.\n- Arcs on a C turn.\n- The composite feed law is a stated assumption about Fanuc-style controls, to be confirmed on a real control.\n- The shipped millturn.mch states no live_tool words, so in-app posting of a C op refuses by name until the user's machine file states them.\n- Size: `post/src/post/mod.rs` (465 -> 483) and `fanuc-lathe.cps` (424 -> ~520) were already over the 400-line target and grew.\n\nChangelog: Continuous C-axis live tooling: rotary kinds on a mill-turn's spindle C state the C angle per move, split to tolerance, and post through the Fanuc lathe post (X Z C under G98 with the machine's live_tool words); every post without liveTooling refuses by name\n\nRefs #33 (first slice: generates, verifies and posts; the owed list above stays on the issue)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
